    "narrative": "With the 2026 season reaching its crescendo on October 13, the Austin Waves are navigating a light schedule. **Brayan Rocchio** serves as our primary offensive engine today, though he sits at a marginal 40.89 score against Freddy Peralta. While Peralta\u2019s 4.32 xERA provides a sliver of hope for production, **Brayan Rocchio** is hampered by his assumed ninth-spot placement in the order and a slight negative platoon dynamic against the right-handed arm. We are banking on his recent form and the park factors to carry him into utility value, but he remains a volatile piece of the puzzle given the scarcity of stolen base threats currently available in our active rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the coaching staff involved **Liam Hicks**, who finished just outside the starting threshold with a 32.11 score. While **Liam Hicks** benefits from a theoretical clean-up spot, he was neutralized by the opposing matchup against Parker Messick. Facing a left-handed arm with a solid 3.51 xERA creates a significant platoon disadvantage, causing the optimizer to relegate him to the bench. Elsewhere, we are dealing with a silent locker room: **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** are unavailable due to team off-days, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined, leaving us to manage roster caps carefully while waiting for high-leverage opportunities from the likes of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Andy Pages** in upcoming slates. We continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias** to ensure no late-breaking lineup changes force a pivot.",
